# Defensive PostgreSQL SQL

## NULL Handling

Always handle NULLs explicitly. Never assume columns have values.

```sql
-- ❌ BAD: NULL comparison fails silently
where status != 'Closed'

-- ✅ GOOD: Explicit NULL handling
where true
    and status is distinct from 'Closed'

-- ✅ GOOD: coalesce for defaults
select coalesce(status, 'Unknown') as status
```

## Column Quoting

PostgreSQL is case-sensitive for quoted identifiers. Quote columns with special characters:

```sql
-- ❌ BAD: Will fail or match wrong column
select fields__status__name

-- ✅ GOOD: Quoted identifier
select "fields__status__name"
```

## Type Casting (PostgreSQL Syntax)

```sql
-- ✅ PostgreSQL casting
id::text
created_at::date
value::numeric

-- ❌ Wrong: Snowflake/BigQuery style
to_varchar(id)
date(created_at)
```

## Date Differences (PostgreSQL)

```sql
-- ❌ Wrong: datediff is Snowflake/Redshift
datediff('day', start_date, end_date)

-- ✅ PostgreSQL: Subtract dates directly (returns integer days)
end_date::date - start_date::date

-- ✅ PostgreSQL: EXTRACT for precision
extract(epoch from end_timestamp - start_timestamp) / 86400.0
```

## Safe Division

```sql
-- ❌ BAD: Division by zero error
revenue / count

-- ✅ GOOD: nullif prevents division by zero
revenue / nullif(count, 0)
```

## Index Recommendations

For large tables, suggest indexes in post-hooks:

```sql
{{
    config(
        materialized='table',
        post_hook=[
            "create index if not exists idx_{{ this.name }}_item_key on {{ this }} (item_key)",
            "create index if not exists idx_{{ this.name }}_as_of_date on {{ this }} (as_of_date)"
        ]
    )
}}
```

## JSONB Extraction (if applicable)

```sql
-- Extract from JSONB
raw_json->>'field_name'              -- as text
(raw_json->>'numeric_field')::int    -- cast after extraction
raw_json->'nested'->'field'          -- nested access
```
